## LGPL obligations (FFmpeg, LAME)

FFmpeg and LAME are distributed under the **GNU Lesser General Public
License, version 2.1 or later**. When you ship an application that uses
them, you must:

1. **Link dynamically.** This package builds FFmpeg shared
   (`--enable-shared --disable-static`). If you ever statically link an LGPL
   library, you must additionally provide the object files of your
   application so users can re-link against a modified version of the
   library.
2. **Bundle the LGPL text** with your application (`licenses/FFmpeg/`).
3. **Display an attribution notice**, for example in an About / Credits
   screen: "This software uses libraries from the FFmpeg project under the
   LGPLv2.1, and from the LAME project under the LGPLv2.1+."
4. **Document modifications.** The patches applied to each component are
   listed in its component record (`pedigree.patches`); the modified source
   must be made available on request.
5. **Do not strip symbol information** beyond what the package already does.
   Users must be able to re-link.

